#pragma rhoform-syntax 0.1

# Before 0.3 `supply` is a name, and a broken line it heads is diagnosed as
# 0.1 reads it: at `out`, asking for what may follow a name, not for the
# `within` or `at` of a 0.3 `supply` statement.
module Rail:
    supply = new rhoform.lib.passive.Resistor(resistance = 1kohm)
    supply out ~ vout
